  "implementation": [
    "Reuse the existing eight-row single-vector kernel for F32/F16/BF16 tensors when columns are a nonzero multiple of four",
    "Read little-endian F32 rows directly from validated mapped bytes, including unaligned offsets, using the physical row stride and the existing 2048-element span boundaries",
    "Use existing Q.Decode_Blocks and bounded workspace for F16/BF16 and retain per-row refusals; preserve quantized batch dispatch and all odd-width fallback paths",
    "Keep exact widened-binary32 FMA, four-lane folding, physical weights and model loop count; no precision change, persistent allocation, new runtime or threads"
  ],
