  "exact_test": "Eight-format old-row/batched-row tests cover row counts 1\u20139/15/16/17; widths 64/256/257/1152/2048/2049/2304/4608; shifted bounds, unaligned weights, partial ranges and untouched outputs. Floating formats exercise Count=1 and unchanged Count=4 fallback, including odd widths; quantized formats retain all counts through 129. Extreme-input scalar comparisons now cover Q8_0/F32/F16/BF16 across all existing row groups and selected batch counts, including maximum finite values, subnormals, cancellation and signed zeros.",
  "equivalence_domain": "Finite widened binary32 multiplicands preserve the existing exact FMA argument. Every F32 direct-read span is checked with Has_Room across all eight physical rows; unsupported widths and formats retain existing execution. No NaN payload equivalence claim.",
